# There was no .dockerignore, so every `docker build .` shipped the whole checkout to the
# daemon: a 34 MB Windows .venv, .git, .superpowers/, artifacts/ and the 1.7 MB kit clone.
# The IMAGE was never affected by this -- the Dockerfile COPYs only pyproject.toml,
# README.md and src, verified by reading it -- so this file is build-time and hygiene, not
# a packaging fix. Do not read its absence as evidence the venv was being baked in.
.venv/
.git/
.github/
artifacts/
.superpowers/
Sentinel_Starter_Kit/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pdf
docs/
tests/
dashboard/
redteam/
scripts/
examples/
